      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T07:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If member has been found in InqDb, does it make sense to enable discovery later on in `CsisActiveDiscovery()`?",
      "revId": "350599c96760521f9e01344ba15389230e8312fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6cb4028b_562c104e",
        "filename": "system/bta/csis/csis_client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T20:08:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have a clear opinion here. I think it shouldn\u0027t hurt.\nIf we finish pairing with another device in set, we should stop the scan.\n\nI think this should stay for case where device in set uses RPA, and just rotated it\u0027s address while we were pairing to 1st set member. This shouldn\u0027t happen often, but it\u0027s possibility.",
      "parentUuid": "e95e665c_0c36d1d8",
      "revId": "350599c96760521f9e01344ba15389230e8312fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da00f2b1_899ccfa6",
        "filename": "system/bta/csis/csis_client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-31T08:34:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think line 1163 comes here with a help. Idea behind CSIS search is that we search for the member and if found we notify Java and wait for this device to be paired.\nWhen paired, and there is still member missing, we will restart active scan.\n\nSo I suggest to make this function return bool and when member is found, just wait for the found member to be paired",
      "parentUuid": "6cb4028b_562c104e",
      "revId": "350599c96760521f9e01344ba15389230e8312fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69f2823f_8e6902c9",
        "filename": "system/bta/csis/csis_client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T21:06:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So in case device rotated address or is just somehow gone, we would now wait 30 seconds (bond attempt timeout) before attempting to scan for it ?\n\nI\u0027m not sure what is worse in this case. If we enable scanning, we might just sightly decrease the initial connection speed (see aosp/2210955 ), so I\u0027m more leaning towards that.",
      "parentUuid": "da00f2b1_899ccfa6",
      "revId": "350599c96760521f9e01344ba15389230e8312fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
